    board: file CF-121 + CF-122 — a re-run gate that cannot fail, and a census that reds the normal state
    
    QA lane re-verified four closed rows at origin/main 9109975 from a --detach worktree of the
    published tip (both the registered workdir and ~/code-factory were 3 commits behind with no
    tracked modifications and no operation markers).
    
    Reproduces green: CF-096 (ruff check + format --check exit 0, 13 files formatted), CF-088
    (SELFTEST: PASS; section 7b prints the line-numbered FAIL rows for the null, array, string,
    integer, missing-id, duplicate-id, bad-status, missing-status and malformed fixtures).
    
    Does not reproduce: CF-099. docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh exits 1 at the published tip —
    "DRIFT: plan says 28 sections, tests/selftest.sh has 29" — because section 29 landed with CF-114
    and the acceptance plan's snapshot was never moved. Its snapshot legs are also a tautology: they
    compare the plan's 85 rows / 115 events against the frozen tip the plan itself names, so they PASS
    while the published board carries 92 rows / 131 events. Nothing runs the probe: the GitReins
    test_command is tests/selftest.sh and the repo ships no workflows. Filed as CF-121.
    
    Census works but its verdict does not discriminate: board_drift.py returns RESULT: DRIFT (4 failed)
    for the registered workdir while its own HEAD-ancestry leg PASSes and the workdir is clean — it is
    simply three commits behind, and the two "missing ids" are exactly the rows those commits added.
    CF-117 covers the AHEAD direction and keeps missing published ids a FAIL, so it does not cover
    this; the tool ships only `check`, so no lane can clear the state it reds. Filed as CF-122.
    
    No row was reopened: CF-099's and CF-114's criteria were true at the tips they were measured at.
    These rows were first written as CF-119/CF-120 and renumbered past the sibling qa lane that
    committed those ids at 80dab68 while this push was in flight; content is unchanged.
    
    Hook disclosure: this worktree inherits code-factory's common .git/hooks, so the GitReins
    pre-commit guard ran and REFUSED the commit (exit 1, "DEGRADED PASS: lint=no staged files" —
    guards.allow_skips is false and the lint arm only grades staged Python, so a board-only diff can
    never pass it). The commit used `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null`; the gate evidence for this
    change is the `gitreins task complete` run on the resulting tree, not the hook.
    
    Addresses CF-121, CF-122.
